<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Seven strike to halt golf coverage.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Seven strike to halt golf coverage.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Television network, The Seven Network Ltd, said a 24 hour strike by workers in Melbourne starting later on Wednesday would stop coverage of the first day of the Greg Norman Golf Classic.</p>
<p>&quot;We won't be able to show the first day of the golf,&quot; Seven's publicity manager Lindy Anderson told Reuters.</p>
<p>She said, however, that Seven's news and entertainment programming would not be affected by the Melbourne strike and had not been affected by a similar 24 hour strike by Sydney workers which started on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Seven would have broadcast the golf tournament for most of Thursday before normal evening programming.</p>
<p>The workers are striking over Seven's proposal for further job losses.</p>
<p>-- Bernard Hickey, Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1812</p>
